      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. it's a good start but honestly i think it's a bit too brief for the \"comprehensive\" level i'm looking for. the score for that one was pretty low because of the length, and i really want these guides to be the gold standard for the students.\n\ncan you do a much, much more in-depth version of the Heisenberg explanation? try to expand on the mathematical derivation, the role of non-commuting operators, and the implications for wave packets. i really need a high word count here to make it worth the students' time, but again, please keep it meaningful. don't just repeat the same sentences over and over, actually go deep into the physics.",
